<figure id="S3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>The results of the CL curriculum, averaged over the three permutations (<math id="S3.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> standard deviation). Since WER is used as a performance measure, some metric interpretations are reversed, e.g., positive BWT scores indicate forgetting. We mark the optimal direction next to the name. <span id="S3.T3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Joint</span> denotes the joint training baseline, and <span id="S3.T3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FT</span> the sequential fine-tuning baseline. </figcaption>
